---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "Does Ophira PDF save changes directly into my original PDF file?",
    answer: "Yes! When Auto-Save is toggled ON (or whenever you click 'Save to File' or press Ctrl+S), your annotations, highlights, form inputs, and ink signatures are written directly back to your local PDF file without having to rename or duplicate it."
  },
  {
    question: "What is the difference between the Setup Installer and Portable edition?",
    answer: "The Windows Setup Installer sets up desktop shortcuts, start menu entries, and file associations with a clean uninstaller. The Portable edition is a single standalone .exe that requires no installation and can be run straight from a USB thumb drive or your Downloads folder."
  },
  {
    question: "Are my documents secure and private?",
    answer: "100%. Ophira PDF operates entirely on your local machine with zero telemetry, zero analytics, and zero cloud services. Your sensitive legal contracts, tax documents, and personal files never touch the internet."
  },
  {
    question: "Why does the app close instantly without asking to save?",
    answer: "Traditional PDF readers constantly annoy users with 'Do you want to save before closing?' modal popups. Ophira PDF's continuous auto-save engine safely commits all changes to disk on-the-fly, allowing the app and tabs to close instantly without interruption."
  },
  {
    question: "How is the visual color scheme designed?",
    answer: "Ophira PDF utilizes a signature palette featuring deep indigo (#3A34C4), bright violet (#8A4FFF), near-white lavender surface (#FBFAFF), and sunny yellow accents (#FFC93C) engineered specifically for reduced contrast fatigue and distraction-free document focus."
  }
];
---

<section class="faq-section" id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="badge" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Common Questions</span>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <p>Everything you need to know about Ophira PDF desktop.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-accordion">
      {faqs.map((faq, idx) => (
        <details class="faq-item card" open={idx === 0}>
          <summary class="faq-question">
            <span>{faq.question}</span>
            <svg class="faq-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
              <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline>
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq-section {
    padding: 5rem 0;
  }

  .faq-accordion {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-item {
    padding: 1.25rem 1.75rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .faq-question {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    list-style: none;
    user-select: none;
    color: var(--text-main);
  }

  .faq-question::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-chevron {
    transition: transform 0.25s ease;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  details[open] .faq-chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
    color: var(--brand-start);
  }

  .faq-answer {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding-top: 0.85rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
</style>
